# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository, whatever the contributor's OS.
#
# Cortex is mostly Markdown that an LLM reads and shell that a host project runs. A file
# that flips to CRLF on someone's editor produces whole-file diffs on lines nobody touched,
# and `setup.sh` copying a CRLF template into a host project is a real failure mode.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell must keep LF endings even when checked out on Windows: CRLF breaks the shebang.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
